onaut  only a week after giving his speech on  May 25th Kennedy was on his way to meet  with Khrushchev in Vienna he was in the  middle of some of the most demanding  months of any presidency and he was  facing obstacles in all directions  before and end domestic it is no wonder  that his health took a turn for the  worst that summer he was besieged by  difficulties of extraordinary  proportions and the American public had  no idea of how precarious his health was  he made a recovery of course but there  were even greater challenges ahead and  he would need all his strength to  confront them as we shall see in our  next lecture on the pivotal year of  1962.

